From 6216d7b4b4ca12d910fbcf8c407fb4e7c7591034 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Mirror the tab sheet under a top address bar, and tint the
 status bar.

With the address bar on top, the tab sheet now drops down from below
it instead of filling the gap between the two bars. It is the same
sheet mirrored: the tab count and actions sit under the address bar,
the list follows, and the handle and the current tab's domain are at
the free bottom edge, which has the round corners. Dragging the handle
down opens it to half or full; dragging it up, or an upward over-pull
at the end of the list, settles it at half or closes it. The snap
rules are the same as for the bottom sheet.

With the address bar at the bottom, the status bar is now dimmed with
the scrim while the sheet is open, through the same status bar scrim
hook the browser's own scrim uses, and restored when it closes. The
small gap a full sheet leaves at its far end is now inside the overlay,
so the scrim covers it too; the half and full heights are unchanged.
With the address bar on top, the status bar keeps the address bar's
color, since the address bar is not dimmed.

A fling on the handle now reads its speed from screen positions. In
the handle's own coordinates, which move with the finger, a fling read
as almost no speed, so only the position decided where it settled.

The side drawer is unchanged.

Tested on the Android emulator (Pixel 10 Pro profile).
